   "text": "The SMILES below is my reading of the drawing, built region by region. Two points are less certain than the rest: the chain length, which I counted from the zigzag spacing, and the hydroxyproline stereocentres, which I took to be the standard VHL-ligand configuration rather than deriving from the wedges.\n\n**Left side**\n- A phenyl ring carries an ortho CH2\u2013NH\u2013CH3 group and is bonded to C4 of a thiophene.\n- The thiophene is 2,4-disubstituted. Its C2 carries a CH(CH3) group that links through NH to the quinazoline.\n- The methyl on that CH is drawn on a bold wedge. Assigning CIP priorities (N > thienyl > CH3 > H) gives R.\n\n**Quinazoline core**\n- C4 carries the NH, C2 carries a methyl, C6 and C7 each carry OMe, and C5 is CH.\n- C8 carries the chain.\n\n**Linker**\n- The chain runs from C8 as eight CH2 groups followed by a C(=O), giving a nonanamide.\n- The amide nitrogen is attached to the alpha carbon of tert-leucine.\n- That alpha carbon has a wedged tert-butyl group, which gives S (the L-amino acid).\n\n**Right side**\n- The tert-leucine C=O acylates the nitrogen of a 4-hydroxyproline, which I took as the (2S,4R) standard VHL configuration.\n- The proline C2 carboxamide NH is bonded to CH2 of a para-substituted benzene.\n- The benzene's other end carries a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl group.\n\nSMILES: CNCc1ccccc1-c1csc([C@@H](C)Nc2nc(C)nc3c(CCCCCCCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N4C[C@H](O)C[C@H]4C(=O)NCc4ccc(cc4)-c4scnc4C)c(OC)c(OC)cc23)c1"
